  "religion": {
    "_note": "Ryujin is SYNCRETIC (the Sino-Japanese honji-suijaku BELIEF): the world HOLDS each power to be one being under two faces - a Chinese celestial official (Sinitic name) and a native kami (Japonic name). This is a belief, NOT a naming operation: the temple-namer never concatenates the two faces. Each holy site takes ONE name, chosen by its building type (see naming_rule), so naming costs exactly what a single-pantheon culture costs. Across a province the player sees the celestial face on Miao/Jiin halls and the kami face on Miya/Jinja shrines, and infers they are the same power - the syncretism surfaces through the spread of names, not within any one name. Faces draw on BOTH family_east_asian.json theonym sets; never real gods. Lawful/Neutral; the dragon-powers of sea and storm are especially honored (Ryujo, the dragon-realm).",
    "clergy_ladder": {
      "1": "Doji (acolyte-child)",
      "3": "Shinkan / Daoshi (priest)",
      "5": "Sozu (prelate)",
      "7": "Daisojo (high prelate)",
      "9": "Tendo-shi (master of the heavenly way)"
    },
